\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The same experiment, read two ways. \textbf  {Left:} a standard verify--refine workflow repairs many tasks the baseline fails (blue, above the axis) and destroys many the baseline solves (orange, below), so the net effect (black, 95\% CI)---the quantity the literature reports---is small and can take either sign. \textbf  {Right:} protecting the incumbent answer removes the lower term entirely and the same machinery becomes a small, reliable gain. Frozen test splits, three execution seeds, matched hard budgets; panels share an axis.}}{1}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:decomposition}{{1}{1}{The same experiment, read two ways. \textbf {Left:} a standard verify--refine workflow repairs many tasks the baseline fails (blue, above the axis) and destroys many the baseline solves (orange, below), so the net effect (black, 95\% CI)---the quantity the literature reports---is small and can take either sign. \textbf {Right:} protecting the incumbent answer removes the lower term entirely and the same machinery becomes a small, reliable gain. Frozen test splits, three execution seeds, matched hard budgets; panels share an axis}{figure.1}{}}
